--TEST--
`SecretEntry::of` says what its value **is** rather than what it may be: a plain, a `secret` and a `tainted` string all reach `$value`, and a duration literal and a computed `Duration` both reach `$ttl` — `rule:security/secret-qualifier`, `rule:core-api/shape-rules`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:security/secret-qualifier`: the assignment relation widens onto the
// `secret` bit and narrows through none, so a plain `string` reaches a `secret
// string` parameter and a `secret` one does too. The parameter says what the
// value is; nothing is laundered in either direction.
secret string $token = "hunter2";

// `rule:core-api/shape-rules` R12: the lifetime is a `Core\Time\Duration` and
// never a count, so a literal and a computed duration are one argument written
// two ways rather than two scales a call site has to remember.
array<Core\Cache\SecretEntry> $sweep = [
    Core\Cache\SecretEntry::of($token, 30s),
    Core\Cache\SecretEntry::of("plain", 30s),
    Core\Cache\SecretEntry::of($token, Core\Time\Duration::seconds(30)),
    Core\Cache\SecretEntry::of("plain", Core\Time\Duration::seconds(30)),
];

// Counted over the whole sweep rather than read off a line: each entry matches
// itself and nothing else, so a member that interned one entry against its
// arguments and answered it again for another spelling fails here while still
// printing a plausible row for each call on its own.
int $matches = 0;
foreach ($sweep as Core\Cache\SecretEntry $entry) {
    foreach ($sweep as Core\Cache\SecretEntry $other) {
        if ($entry == $other) {
            $matches = $matches + 1;
        }
    }
}
echo "each spelling built its own entry: ", $matches, " of ", Core\Arr::count($sweep), "\n";

// A secret that came from outside is the ordinary case and not the exception —
// a token a fill fetched came off the wire. `$from` is `string|tainted string`,
// which `Core\Env::get`'s own `$name` sink refuses and this parameter admits;
// what the entry does not do is carry the mark onward, being an object.
var $from = Core\Env::get("NVS_A_SECRET_ENTRY_HAS_NO_SUCH_NAME") ?? "fetched";
var $outside = Core\Cache\SecretEntry::of($from, 30s);
echo "a tainted secret is admitted: ", Core\Reflect::typeOf($outside) == Core\Reflect\TypeKind::Object ? "object" : "other", "\n";
--EXPECT--
each spelling built its own entry: 4 of 4
a tainted secret is admitted: object
